      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "INTRODUCTION",
          "content": "Multiseptate gallbladder is a rare congenital condition that may be asymptomatic or may lead to symptoms consistent with biliary colic, even in the absence of cholelithiasis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "DISCUSSION",
          "content": "We present the case of a 19-year-old female who underwent an extensive gastrointestinal workup before she was referred for cholecystectomy, which led to resolution of her symptoms. The distinct imaging features of this entity are presented."
        }
      ]},
